WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:03.652
What made these gold leaves close?

00:00:03.953 --> 00:00:07.217
The camera sees only the
inside of the cabinet.

00:00:07.742 --> 00:00:14.654
Replay the same moment. Outside, a sheet of
mica slides between two capacitor plates.

00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:22.321
As the overlap grows, capacitance rises. With
charge nearly fixed, the leaves draw together.

00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:28.092
Now read the experiment as the model
does. Seven photographs, in order.

00:00:28.473 --> 00:00:30.443
First, full insertion.

00:00:30.443 --> 00:00:31.803
Then withdrawal.

00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:33.113
Half insertion.

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:34.343
Withdrawal.

00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:35.673
Half insertion.

00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:36.969
Withdrawal.

00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:40.739
The model recovered all six
commands in this trial.

00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:47.483
In another cabinet, three transparent
specimens change colour under polarized light.

00:00:47.787 --> 00:00:52.923
A press changes their load. Rotating
the optics also changes the pattern.

00:00:53.488 --> 00:01:00.016
Across twenty apparatuses, the question is the
same. Which controls produced the evidence?

00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:09.391
GPT-6.1 Sol exact match fell from
83.7% for one event to 68.0% for six.

00:01:09.805 --> 00:01:15.895
At six events, it matched 1,035
individual events out of 1,200,

00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:20.725
but only 136 complete sequences out of 200.

00:01:21.222 --> 00:01:26.022
CaveBench. Reconstructing hidden
events from what they leave behind.

